[38;5;231m⏺[39m Before I write this: [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m permanently deletes the [38;5;153mnotes[39m data for all 48,000 production
  rows. The deploy job applies migrations in order, so once it runs there is no rollback — a down-migration can recreate
  the column but not the contents. "We stopped using it" is the part I need you to confirm, not assume: no reporting
  query, export, or admin view still reads it, and nobody needs the existing values archived first.

  If you confirm, here's exactly what I'd add — nothing else:

  [38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[39m
