  [34mALTER TABLE[39m users [34mDROP[39m [34mCOLUMN[39m notes;

  and remove the [38;5;153mnotes TEXT,[39m line from [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m to keep the mirror in sync (the README says that's maintained by
  hand).

  Two things worth knowing before you say yes:

  - If this is SQLite, [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m needs 3.35+ (2021). Older engines require the rebuild-and-copy dance. Tell me the
    engine if it's not SQLite.
  - If you want the data preserved, the usual move is [38;5;153mCREATE TABLE users_notes_archive AS SELECT id, notes FROM users [39m
    [38;5;153mWHERE notes IS NOT NULL;[39m in the same migration, before the drop. Say the word and I'll include it.

